# Integrates Phase 4 Standards: Timeline, Coordination, Navigation, Error & Quality, Research & Ideas, Audit & Analysis, Architecture

## SUPPORTING STANDARDS (PHASE 4)

### Core Principle: Comprehensive Supporting Documentation
**These rules ensure all supporting documentation types follow consistent standards for coordination, navigation, quality, research, and analysis.**

---

## ⏰ **TIMELINE & HISTORY STANDARDS**

### Timeline Context Entries
- **Purpose:** Event-based timeline tracking with structured context preservation
- **When:** Track significant events, milestones, context changes
- **Format:** Structured entries with timestamp, event type, context, participants
- **Rules:** Use `mcp_lucid-mcp_add_timeline_entry` for timeline tracking

### Build Timeline
- **Purpose:** Visual milestone timeline showing project progress
- **When:** After each milestone, major achievement
- **Format:** Chronological markdown with visual representation
- **Rules:** Include date, milestone, attribution, celebration moments

### Build Ledger
- **Purpose:** Chronological feature log with complete attribution
- **When:** After each feature completion
- **Format:** Dated entries with feature, builder, description
- **Rules:** Complete attribution, chronological order, feature descriptions

---

## 🤝 **COORDINATION & COMMUNICATION STANDARDS**

### Coordination Files
- **Purpose:** AI-to-AI coordination, task tracking, daily logs
- **When:** Multi-agent coordination, task assignment, status updates
- **Format:** Structured coordination documents with assignments, status, blockers
- **Rules:** Clear assignments, status tracking, blocker documentation

### Status Reports
- **Purpose:** Regular progress updates for stakeholders
- **When:** Weekly/monthly reporting, milestone reporting
- **Format:** Structured reports with progress, metrics, blockers, next steps
- **Rules:** Include metrics, progress tracking, issue identification, next actions

### Goal Dashboard
- **Purpose:** Visual goal tracking with at-a-glance status
- **When:** Regular goal tracking, progress visualization
- **Format:** Dashboard format with visual progress indicators
- **Rules:** Clear visual indicators, progress percentages, status at-a-glance

---

## 🧭 **NAVIGATION & INDEXING STANDARDS**

### SUPER_INDEX
- **Purpose:** Master concept map with cross-reference system
- **When:** Creating/updating concept maps, navigation aids
- **Format:** Structured index with concept links, cross-references
- **Rules:** Complete coverage, cross-references, navigation links, maintenance rules

### Hierarchical Navigation Index
- **Purpose:** Nested concept organization with hierarchical browsing
- **When:** Organizing concepts hierarchically, creating navigation structures
- **Format:** Hierarchical structure with nested concepts
- **Rules:** Logical hierarchy, clear nesting, context-aware navigation

---

## 🔍 **ERROR & QUALITY STANDARDS**

### Error Intelligence
- **Purpose:** Error tracking, analysis, pattern detection, prevention
- **When:** Errors occur, error analysis needed, pattern detection
- **Format:** Error logs with analysis, patterns, prevention strategies
- **Rules:** Complete error logging, pattern analysis, prevention documentation

### Test Documentation
- **Purpose:** Test coverage tracking, test results documentation, quality assurance
- **When:** Test creation, test execution, coverage tracking
- **Format:** Test documentation with coverage, results, quality metrics
- **Rules:** Complete test coverage, result documentation, quality tracking

### Quality Metrics
- **Purpose:** Code quality tracking, quality trends, improvement tracking
- **When:** Quality assessment, quality improvement, trend analysis
- **Format:** Metrics with baselines, targets, trends, thresholds
- **Rules:** Regular measurement, trend tracking, threshold monitoring

---

## 💡 **RESEARCH & IDEAS STANDARDS**

### Ideas Registry
- **Purpose:** Idea capture by role, idea organization, evolution tracking
- **When:** Ideas emerge, idea organization needed, idea evolution
- **Format:** Structured registry with idea, role, category, status, evolution
- **Rules:** Complete capture, role attribution, status tracking, evolution documentation

### Research Notes
- **Purpose:** Research findings, external ideas, source tracking
- **When:** Research conducted, external ideas found, sources identified
- **Format:** Structured notes with findings, sources, citations, relevance
- **Rules:** Source attribution, citation tracking, relevance documentation

---

## 📊 **AUDIT & ANALYSIS STANDARDS**

### Audit Reports
- **Purpose:** Comprehensive system audits, quality assessments, compliance checks
- **When:** System audits, quality assessments, compliance verification
- **Format:** Structured audit reports with findings, recommendations, action items
- **Rules:** Complete coverage, findings documentation, actionable recommendations

### Analysis Documents
- **Purpose:** System analysis, performance evaluation, impact assessment
- **When:** System analysis needed, performance evaluation, impact assessment
- **Format:** Structured analysis with methodology, findings, conclusions, recommendations
- **Rules:** Clear methodology, complete findings, actionable conclusions

---

## 🏗️ **ARCHITECTURE STANDARDS**

### Atlas Maps
- **Purpose:** System architecture maps, relationship visualization, component mapping
- **When:** System architecture documentation, relationship mapping, component organization
- **Format:** Structured maps with components, relationships, dependencies
- **Rules:** Complete component coverage, relationship documentation, dependency mapping

### Configuration Files
- **Purpose:** System configuration documentation, setup instructions, parameter tracking
- **When:** Configuration documentation, setup instructions, parameter documentation
- **Format:** Structured configuration with parameters, defaults, descriptions
- **Rules:** Complete parameter documentation, default values, setup instructions

